This class monitors DOM elements that have attributes encoded
to show a tooltip. A single {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip} instance is reused
and reconfigured with the attributes retrieved from the DOM.

Typically, this class will not be created directly, but rather configured
via the application with the {@link Ext.app.Application#cfg!quickTips Ext.app.Application#quickTips} config to
enable this globally.

# Configuring via Ext.Component

A configuration given to a {@link Ext.Component#cfg!tooltip tooltip} config will
be registered with this manager and shared tips will be displayed when that
component is activated. See {@link Ext.Component#cfg!tooltip tooltip} for details.

# Configuring via HTML attributes

A tip may also be configured by adding data attributes to DOM elements. The
following attribute names are supported and map to configurations on the
{@link Ext.tip.ToolTip} class. The following are supported:
- `data-qtip`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!html Ext.tip.ToolTip#html}
- `data-qwidth`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!width Ext.tip.ToolTip#width}
- `data-qminWidth`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!minWidth Ext.tip.ToolTip#minWidth}
- `data-qmaxWidth`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!maxWidth Ext.tip.ToolTip#maxWidth}
- `data-qtitle`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!title Ext.tip.ToolTip#title}
- `data-qautoHide`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!autoHide Ext.tip.ToolTip#autoHide}
- `data-qcls`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!cls Ext.tip.ToolTip#cls}
- `data-qalign`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!align Ext.tip.ToolTip#align}
- `data-qalignDelegate`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!alignDelegate Ext.tip.ToolTip#alignDelegate}
- `data-qanchor`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!anchor Ext.tip.ToolTip#anchor}
- `data-qanchorToTarget`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!anchorToTarget Ext.tip.ToolTip#anchorToTarget}
- `data-qallowOver`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!allowOver Ext.tip.ToolTip#allowOver}
- `data-qshowDelay`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!showDelay Ext.tip.ToolTip#showDelay}
- `data-qhideDelay`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!hideDelay Ext.tip.ToolTip#hideDelay}
- `data-qdismissDelay`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!dismissDelay Ext.tip.ToolTip#dismissDelay}
- `data-qtrackMouse`: {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!trackMouse Ext.tip.ToolTip#trackMouse}
- `data-qoverfow`: Indicates that if the element's text is clipped
using the `text-overflow:ellipsis` style, the shared tip will be shown
containing the `innerHTML`.

Example usage:

    <div class="foo" data-qtip="Message goes here">Hover me</div>
    <p>
    <div
     data-qoverflow="true"
     data-qalign="b-t?"
     data-qanchor="true"
     style="width:100px;text-overflow:ellipsis"
    >
        Hover Me! Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, duis dicta solet
        et qui. Ut mea soleat mediocritatem, blandit democritum mea ex. His id nostro
        conceptam dissentiet, ignota discere id mea. Qui eu virtute invenire, an per
        ipsum invidunt senserit. Ne legendos expetenda mei. Ad homero percipit liberavisse
        quo, te quando vocibus usu.
    </div>

A configuration object to use when the shared tip instance is triggered by
an text-clipped element tagged with the `data-qoverflow` attribute.
For example, you could change the default
{@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!dismissDelay dismissDelay} to be longer, to allow long content
to be read, or set {@link Ext.tip.ToolTip#cfg!autoHide autoHide} to false by setting your
application's {@link Ext.app.Application#cfg!quickTips quickTips} config.

        quickTips: {
            tooltip: {
                showOnTap: true
            },
            overflowTip: {
                dismissDelay: 10000
            }
        }

